</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Judge-panel validation.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Ten legal experts validated the rubric-based judge outputs for Issue Resolution and Inquiry. The reported benchmark runs use the judge identifiers in Table <a href="#A6.T23" title="Table 23 ‣ F.4 Run Configuration ‣ Appendix F Model and Run Details ‣ DLawBench: Evaluating LLMs Through Multi-Turn Legal Consultation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>. The validation uses slice verification against item-level panel verdicts. Table <a href="#A7.T25" title="Table 25 ‣ Judge-panel validation. ‣ G.1 Human Validation Details ‣ Appendix G Evaluation Methodology Details ‣ DLawBench: Evaluating LLMs Through Multi-Turn Legal Consultation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a> summarizes the updated validation sample, and Table <a href="#A7.T26" title="Table 26 ‣ Judge-panel validation. ‣ G.1 Human Validation Details ‣ Appendix G Evaluation Methodology Details ‣ DLawBench: Evaluating LLMs Through Multi-Turn Legal Consultation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a> reports panel-vs-human-majority accuracy, human pairwise accuracy, and chance-corrected agreement.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.T25" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 25: </span>Coverage of the updated judge-panel human validation sample for rubric dimensions.</figcaption>
<table id="A7.T25.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
